From: SM-X910 postmarketOS port <gts9uwifi@example.com>
Subject: [PATCH] phy: snps-eusb2: match downstream SM8550 PLL setup

The SM-X910 reaches DWC3 gadget mode with the upstream SM8550 eUSB2 PHY
sequence, but the host cannot read its USB descriptor. Samsung's working
SM8550 driver waits after asserting POR and programs CPBIAS to one, whereas
the upstream sequence has no delay and writes zero.

Reproduce those two hardware sequencing details from the working downstream
driver. The remaining PLL and transmitter values already match upstream.

---
 drivers/phy/phy-snps-eusb2.c | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/phy/phy-snps-eusb2.c b/drivers/phy/phy-snps-eusb2.c
index af4fa17ac1ab..f86d5181f3fb 100644
--- a/drivers/phy/phy-snps-eusb2.c
+++ b/drivers/phy/phy-snps-eusb2.c
@@ -372,6 +372,8 @@ static int qcom_snps_eusb2_hsphy_init(struct phy *p)
 				    CMN_CTRL_OVERRIDE_EN, CMN_CTRL_OVERRIDE_EN);
 
 	snps_eusb2_hsphy_write_mask(phy->base, QCOM_USB_PHY_UTMI_CTRL5, POR, POR);
+	/* Match Samsung SM8550 sequencing before enabling the PHY. */
+	usleep_range(10, 20);
 
 	snps_eusb2_hsphy_write_mask(phy->base, QCOM_USB_PHY_HS_PHY_CTRL_COMMON0,
 				    PHY_ENABLE | RETENABLEN, PHY_ENABLE | RETENABLEN);
@@ -391,7 +393,7 @@ static int qcom_snps_eusb2_hsphy_init(struct phy *p)
 
 	snps_eusb2_hsphy_write_mask(phy->base, QCOM_USB_PHY_CFG_CTRL_1,
 				    PHY_CFG_PLL_CPBIAS_CNTRL_MASK,
-				    FIELD_PREP(PHY_CFG_PLL_CPBIAS_CNTRL_MASK, 0x0));
+				    FIELD_PREP(PHY_CFG_PLL_CPBIAS_CNTRL_MASK, 0x1));
 
 	snps_eusb2_hsphy_write_mask(phy->base, QCOM_USB_PHY_CFG_CTRL_4,
 				    PHY_CFG_PLL_INT_CNTRL_MASK,
-- 
2.50.1
